# /etc/xdg/user-dirs.defaults — W Linux: the standard folders of a home directory.
#
# Read by xdg-user-dirs-update at every login (xdg-user-dirs.service). Each value
# is a path relative to the home and is TRANSLATED element by element into the
# user's language through gettext (~/Pictures on an English system is
# ~/Изображения on a Russian one), then recorded in ~/.config/user-dirs.dirs —
# which is what programs read (`xdg-user-dir PICTURES`). Names are never hard-
# coded anywhere in W for that reason; see w-userdirs.md.
#
# W ships six of upstream's nine. TEMPLATES (GNOME's "New document" menu) and
# PUBLICSHARE (a personal file share) have no consumer on this desktop, and
# PROJECTS (new in xdg-user-dirs 0.20) would plant a folder W has no opinion
# about into every home. A folder that is not listed simply is not created;
# `xdg-user-dir TEMPLATES` then answers with the home itself, which is the
# spec's own fallback. Shadows the package's copy (pacman keeps ours and writes
# its own as .pacnew).
DESKTOP=Desktop
DOWNLOAD=Downloads
DOCUMENTS=Documents
MUSIC=Music
PICTURES=Pictures
VIDEOS=Videos
